<title>FRANCE: Rouen May 1-28 grain exports at 494,171 tonnes.</title>
<headline>Rouen May 1-28 grain exports at 494,171 tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Grain exports from the French port of Rouen reached 494,171 tonnes between May 1 and May 28, port officials said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Grain exports were 174,000 tonnes for the whole of May 1996.</p>
<p>The May 1-28 grain total included 348,321 tonnes of wheat and 145,850 tonnes of barley.</p>
<p>Officials gave the following breakdown by destination (in tonnes).</p>
<p>WHEAT</p>
<p>    West Africa		   79,055</p>
<p>    Algeria			 22,700</p>
<p>    Britain			 16,400</p>
<p>    Ireland			  4,615</p>
<p>    Italy			  173,531</p>
<p>    Morocco			 15,000</p>
<p>    Portugal			 3,300</p>
<p>    La Reunion island	    3,000</p>
<p>    Turkey			  30,720</p>
<p>BARLEY</p>
<p>    South Africa		  24,800</p>
<p>    Saudi Arabia		  59,700</p>
<p>    Argentina		     25,000</p>
<p>    Greece			   3,000</p>
<p>    Italy			    2,350</p>
<p>    Tunisia			 25,000</p>
<p>    Turkey			   6,000</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
